.TH UDR 1 "" "udr 0.9.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
udr \- rsync over UDT
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B udr
.RI [ "UDR options" ]
.B rsync
.RI [ "rsync options" ]
.I source destination
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B udr
runs rsync with its data channel on UDT, a reliable transport on UDP, in
place of ssh. One side is local and one remote:
.IR host:path " or " user@host:path .
.PP
udr logs in to the remote host with ssh and starts udr there. The remote udr
picks a free UDP port from a range and reports it over the ssh connection;
the transfer then runs over that port. udr must be installed on both hosts.
.PP
The rsync options are rsync's own, except
.BR \-e " and " \-\-rsh ,
which udr sets.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-P " ssh-port"
Port of the remote ssh server (default 22).
.TP
.BI \-a " port"
First UDP port the receiving host may use (default 9000).
.TP
.BI \-b " port"
Last UDP port it may use (default 9100).
.TP
.BI \-c " path"
Path of udr on the remote host (default: udr, from the remote PATH).
.TP
.BI \-d " seconds"
Data transfer timeout (default 15).
.TP
.BI \-r " Mbps"
Cap the sending rate.
.TP
.BI \-i " address"
Address the receiver binds to.
.TP
.BR \-n [\fIcipher\fR]
Encrypt the data channel. The cipher goes right after the option, as in
.BR \-naes\-256 ;
udr hands the remote side no cipher name it reads, so every connection runs
aes\-128. See
.BR SECURITY .
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH FIREWALL
The receiving host takes inbound UDP on one port per transfer running at the
same time, from the \-a to \-b range. The sending host needs nothing beyond
replies to what it started. With
.B \-a 9000 \-b 9000
exactly one port is open and one transfer can run.
.SH SECURITY
Without \-n the data channel is plain. With \-n it uses one key for both
directions, an all-zero IV and a stream mode, and nothing authenticates the
packets. Treat it as obfuscation and run udr inside a tunnel (WireGuard,
ssh \-w) when the data matters. ssh protects the login only.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
udr rsync \-av \-\-progress /data/ host:/data/
udr \-P 27522 \-a 9000 \-b 9000 rsync \-a big.tar user@host:/srv/
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rsync (1),
.BR ssh (1)
